     "text": "Morgan-Wong Medical Group\nRe: Carrie Gregory (DOB 03/30/1966)\n\n---\n\nJanuary 17, 2025: Carrie Gregory visited today to receive her flu shot. During the visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 128/82 and her weight was 155 pounds. She continues to be under care for her known NAFLD, also known as fatty liver disease, with fibrosis classified as F3. Her condition has been managed well and remains controlled.\n\n---\n\nAugust 15, 2024: Carrie Gregory came in today for a follow-up regarding her NAFLD / fatty liver. Her blood pressure was measured at 122/79 and her weight at 160 pounds. As previously noted, she has NAFLD with fibrosis stage F3. Her condition is currently stable and under control.\n\n---\n\nMarch 12, 2024: Carrie Gregory was seen today for an evaluation of her NAFLD / fatty liver. Her blood pressure was 122/72 and she weighed 158 pounds at the time of the visit. Carrie’s NAFLD is well-managed, with fibrosis staged at F3. She continues to do well with her treatment plan.\n\n---\n\nOctober 09, 2023: Carrie Gregory visited today specifically for monitoring her NAFLD / fatty liver. She reported feeling well and fine. Her blood pressure was 129/71 and her weight was 158 pounds. Her NAFLD remains stable, with fibrosis classified as F3. There have been no new developments or complications reported.\n\n---\n\nMay 06, 2023: Carrie Gregory was seen today for her routine check-up related to her NAFLD / fatty liver. At that time, her blood pressure was 123/79 and her weight was 150 pounds. Her NAFLD, with fibrosis at stage F3, is well managed, and she continues to follow her prescribed treatment plan.\n\n---\n\nDecember 01, 2022: Carrie Gregory visited us on December 1, 2022, for a follow-up related to her NAFLD / fatty liver. Her blood pressure at that visit was 122/79, and she weighed 149 pounds. Her NAFLD, with fibrosis classified as F3, is being effectively managed. She continues to adhere to her treatment regimen.\n\n---\n\nSocial History: Carrie has a history of tobacco use, having smoked cigarettes at a rate of 10 per day. She began smoking on October 24, 1989, and quit on October 19, 2023. She was honest about her smoking history.\n\nFamily History: Carrie’s father passed away at the age of 47 due to a myocardial infarction (MI). Her brother also died suddenly from a cardiac event at the age of 52. Her mother had a myocardial infarction the age 65 and passed away at 88 years old.\n\n---\n\nDr. Michelle Franklin\nGastroenterologist\nMorgan-Wong Medical Group\n\n[End of Record]\n"
